  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.12.0: ChromaConfigurationOptions.WithUpsertStrategy says how UpdateAsync and UpsertAsync write the embeddings of records that exist, for Chroma 1.0.21 to 1.5.9, which may lose a record from the vector index after such a write; on the server, RAYON_NUM_THREADS=1 avoided it in our measurements. Server, the default, writes as before. SkipUnchangedEmbeddings updates without the embedding a record whose embedding does not change, which does not touch the vector index; it costs a get of the records first. The creation of a collection sends get_or_create once. All the releases: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client/releases. Tested versions: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client/blob/main/docs/COMPATIBILITY.md. Migration from 1.x: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client#migrating-from-chromadbclient-1x",
